.TH "MAKNOON" "1" "Jan 2024" "Maknoon Post-Quantum Engine" "Maknoon Manual"

.SH NAME
maknoon-reencrypt - Re-encrypt a file with a different cryptographic profile


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon reencrypt  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Re-encrypt an existing .makn file using a different profile ID.

.PP
The file is decrypted using its current profile, then immediately re-encrypted
with the target profile. This enables migration from the default NIST profile (1)
to the conservative non-lattice profile (3) or any custom profile.

.PP
Example:
  maknoon reencrypt secret.makn --profile 3 --passphrase oldpass


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dir\fP[=false]
	Reencrypt all .makn files in a directory (recursive)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	List files that would be reencrypted without doing it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reencrypt

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	Output file path (default: overwrite input in-place)

.PP
\fB--passphrase\fP=""
	Passphrase (omit for interactive prompt)

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=3
	Target profile ID (1=NIST, 3=Conservative/FrodoKEM)

.PP
\fB--workers\fP=4
	Parallel worker count for directory reencrypt


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB--passphrase-fd\fP=0
	Read passphrase from file descriptor N (e.g., --passphrase-fd 3  3<<<$(pass show key)). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FD

.PP
\fB--passphrase-file\fP=""
	Read passphrase from a file instead of prompting (use - for stdin). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FILE

.PP
\fB--policy\fP=""
	Path to a declarative governance policy file (JSON)

.PP
\fB--tpm\fP[=false]
	Enable TPM 2.0 hardware-backed storage for keys

.PP
\fB--tpm-device\fP="/dev/tpmrm0"
	Path to the TPM device node

.PP
\fB--tpm-pcrs\fP=[]
	List of PCRs to bind keys to (e.g., 7,14)

.PP
\fB--trace\fP[=false]
	Enable low-level diagnostic tracing to stderr


